197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (Beyond France, the Community Supported Agriculture \(CSA\) model is a thriving global movement, particularly well-established in North America, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland. While the French Cocagne network places a unique emphasis on socio-professional reintegration, international actors often focus on direct-to-consumer \(D2C\) organic distribution, regenerative agriculture, and building robust local food systems.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
198 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (From a technological standpoint, these foreign initiatives frequently leverage highly advanced digital ecosystems. Instead of traditional administrative setups, international CSA farms often use seamless e-commerce subscription engines, dynamic harvest previews, and integrated community solidarity features \(such as "Pay it forward" micro-donations\). To provide a comprehensive benchmark, this report also evaluates several international farms to compare their digital strategies and identify best IT practices in the global organic market.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
