/E (The shift towards sustainable agriculture depends not only on green farming practices but also on reliable and easy-to-use digital tools. Local food networks such as Community-Supported Agriculture \(CSA\) in English-speaking countries and AMAPs or Jardins de Cocagne in France rely heavily on their websites to attract new members, manage harvests, organize deliveries, and process regular payments.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (This report analyzes how these community-based farms use web technologies. By looking at how their websites are built specifically focusing on mobile design, the user journey, and account login systems this study highlights the digital roadblocks that frustrate users and prevent them from subscribing. Finally, it compares these local platforms to successful international examples to show how the digital experience can be improved.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
