/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (The Great Day Gardens website combines the farm's presentation, its CSA program and its online shop within the same website. This creates a relatively consistent user experience because customers do not need to leave the main website to access the shop. The website also provides information about pickup locations and allows customers to place orders online.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (The CSA system is based on a farmer's-choice model. Customers receive a selection of vegetables chosen by the farm rather than selecting every product themselves. The website also allows members to purchase additional products such as bread, eggs, flowers and other products. The 2026 CSA requires payment at the beginning of the season, and customers receive electronic invoices that can be paid using several methods, including ACH, cash, check or credit card.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (The online shop uses a standard e-commerce structure, with products organized into categories and individual product pages. Customers can therefore purchase products separately from their CSA membership. The website also provides several pickup options, which makes the ordering process relatively practical.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (However, the website remains relatively simple from a technical point of view. The CSA system focuses mainly on registration and payment rather than offering advanced subscription management. Customers cannot freely customize the contents of their weekly CSA share because the farm uses a farmer's-choice model. The website also provides limited advanced search or filtering features for the online catalogue.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
